    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Tools from someone who's done the job</h1>
    <p class="lead">ELA Class 3-8 makes reading and intervention resources for grades 3&ndash;8 classrooms and for the people who run intervention: literacy interventionists, reading specialists and SPED case managers.</p>

    <p>Everything here started as something that had to exist for a real classroom or caseload. The store is built and run by a 25-year educator with dual master's degrees in Educational Technology and Educational Administration, and every resource is designed to be technically correct first and pretty second, because the people using these tools are specialists who notice when something is wrong.</p>

    <h2>Two lines</h2>
    <p><strong>Indiana ILEARN ELA</strong> is test practice for grades 3&ndash;8: one set for each of the three Checkpoints and the Summative, with a free screener for each checkpoint. Every passage and item is original, written to Indiana's published standards, blueprint and item specifications, and every answer key explains every wrong answer. <a href="/indiana-ela/">See the ELA line &rarr;</a></p>
    <p><strong>Mapped &amp; Managed</strong> is where the store started. <em>Mapped</em> is the literacy side: explicit decoding routines, like syllable division and multisyllabic word reading for older readers. <em>Managed</em> is the documentation side: keeping IEP data, goals, caseloads and tier decisions organized and defensible. <a href="/shop/">See Mapped &amp; Managed &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2>Mapped &amp; Managed's four lanes</h2>
    <ul class="checks" style="--accent:{{ site.colors.sage }}">
      <li><strong>Mapped Literacy</strong>: multisyllabic decoding and syllable division for grades 3&ndash;8.</li>
      <li><strong>Managed IEP</strong>: IEP documentation and progress monitoring.</li>
      <li><strong>Teacher Systems</strong>: scheduling, planning and tracking for interventionists.</li>
      <li><strong>Managed MTSS</strong>: screening, tiering, progress monitoring and attendance for RTI/MTSS teams.</li>
    </ul>

